            "text": "How whirls the wind!\nHow speeds the carriage!\nI look back upon the great road,\nAnd my heart is full of grief.\n\nHow blows the wind!\nHow the carriage hurries!\nI look back upon the great road,\nAnd my heart is sad.\n\nWho can cook the fish?\nLet him wash the pot.\nWho is going west?\nLet him carry kind words."
